The search results confirm that the Mercedes-Benz 500 SEL was a variant of the W126 S-Class sedan produced from 1980 to 1991 (Source 1, 3, 5, 7, 9). The "SEL" designation indicated a long wheelbase and fuel injection ("Einspritzmotor" and "L" for long wheelbase) (Source 1). While the S-Class line has continued through several generations (W140, W220, W221, W222, W223), the specific "500 SEL" designation is associated with the vintage W126 model and is not used for a currently produced vehicle (Source 7, 10, 12). Current S-Class models use designations like S 500 or S 580 (Source 12).

Since the requested model ("most recent version of Mercedes-Benz 500 SEL") refers to a historical model and not a specific, currently produced vehicle in today's market, the data is ambiguous for the purpose of scoring against current benchmarks.

